      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd like to see some addition warnings/auto-fixes for these differences between WD On and Off since they can make what looks like a simple conversion from On to Off much more annoying without prior knowledge of them:\n• When a WD Off state has no animation.\nSuch states tend to break things. I'm not actually sure what the intended or resulting behaviour is of a WD Off state with no animation, it almost seems to not stop the animation from the previous state when transitioned to.\nI always use an 'empty' animation (2 keyframes that animate a shape key of a mesh that doesn't exist) to avoid the issues of WD Off states without animations.\n• When non-humanoid Gesture Playable Layer animations are used and there is a WD Off state in a layer in FX that doesn't have an Avatar Mask that prevents the transforms that are animated in the Gesture Playable Layer.\nIf you're animating transforms in the Gesture Playable Layer, any layer in FX that has WD Off states (with an animation) will prevent the animations of transforms in the Gesture Playable Layer from working, unless the layer in FX also has an Avatar Mask that prevents the transforms (used by the Gesture Playable Layer) from being used.\n--\nHai has consolidated a ton of highly useful information on using WD Off and its quirks: https://hai-vr.github.io/combo-gesture-expressions-av3/writedefaults.html",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
