  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-05T13:35:06.951Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the latest dev blog, it’s clear that avatar animators with write defaults on will break even more in future updates. However, write defaults on is the Unity default; not only would you not know that it’s discouraged unless you go digging through the documentation, but even if you intend for it to be off it’s very easy to accidentally leave it enabled. The sdk should have guardrails to help protect against this, e.g.:\n* alter the editor default to the recommended off state\n* show an upload warning when it’s left on \n* add an auto fix to generate a layer with the default states to then FX layer and then disable all write defaults states",
